{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922815-boston-inspirations-and-music","id":922815,"title":"Boston Inspirations and Music","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-28T13:23:45-07:00","id":922815,"title":"Boston Inspirations and Music","content":"I'm starting to run <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827351#post827351\"><b>Mage</b> 2E game in Boston, Massachusetts</a>. After today's literal first session I understand I do not 'feel' this city the way I get London, for example. Clearly I need some local ( and probably dark ) inspirations and music for <b>CoD</b>-like vibe to put it in there. Any help will be much appreciated. Boston is written as mostly<b> Mage </b>setting. but I need more general and 'dark/horror' feel of this metropolis than strictly magical one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:28:52-07:00","id":922882,"title":"","content":"Dropkick Murphys is pretty ubiquitously Boston, but they're more punk than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:30:43-07:00","id":923114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922815-boston-inspirations-and-music?p=922882#post922882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dropkick Murphys is pretty ubiquitously Boston, but they're more punk than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sound very... Irish. Are you telling me the Boston is about being Green Clovers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Punk can be good - it would work for combat and actions scenes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T06:09:26-07:00","id":923203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922815-boston-inspirations-and-music?p=923114#post923114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They sound very... Irish. Are you telling me the Boston is about being Green Clovers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Punk can be good - it would work for combat and actions scenes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Boston has a pretty big Irish-American population. Hence the Irish influence of their sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T06:25:30-07:00","id":923209,"title":"","content":"Are there other 'major ethnical influances' I should look over?<br /> <br /> I watched couple of Bostonian TV series - like <b>Boston Public </b>and <b>Fringe</b> - but I found black actors are minority in those production. ( Beside Chi McBride, but even his surname is Irish... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T07:04:43-07:00","id":923225,"title":"","content":"Have you watched The Departed? It's a street-level, Boston-based thriller with lots of references to organized crime, ethnic conflicts and state corruption. Also, an excellent film in its own right. <br /> <br /> I don't know much about music inspiration, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:04:16-07:00","id":923256,"title":"","content":"Along with the Departed, Boondock Saints is another possible source of inspiration, being set in Boston, and with a heavy Irish-Catholic cultural influence. <br /> <br /> With the Red Sox, Bruins, and Celtics, and Patriots, Boston is a sports heavy city, i.e. 90% of the time if you go into a bar, that's what will be playing instead of music. Bostonians hate New York. Publicly supporting the Yankees in particular can get you in bar fights.<br /> <br /> Reaching out to the regional sense, Boston isn't so much of a Metropolis like NYC or London. Rather, it's more of a central hub to a number of suburban areas. Many people who work in Boston don't live in Boston. They live in Cambridge, in Somerville, in Watertown, in Weymouth, etc. If someone says they are from a town you haven't heard of, there's a good chance they'll follow the name of their town with &quot;It's just outside Boston.&quot; Boston proper has plenty of neighborhoods though. Southie (south boston) is particularly considered to be a rough section.<br /> <br /> People in Boston think that the state ends just west of Worcester (pronounced 'Wuss-ter'), which is half an hour west of Boston. You might want to look into how the names of towns are pronounced if you aren't familiar with the area. <br /> <br /> Boston is one of the oldest cities in the US, and so appropriately has a lot of ghost stories and local legends. Salem, of the witch trials fame, isn't far, and many events of the early Revolutionary War happened near or in Boston.<br /> <br /> Hope some of this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T20:00:43-07:00","id":930668,"title":"","content":"Thanks for help for now!<br /> <br /> Need some help with plot idea I got - For it to work, I need to use construction site of new building. Place need to be under architects regular supervision. <b>What kind of buildings like those are build in Boston now and where on it's map?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T23:04:31-07:00","id":930730,"title":"","content":"Does it have to be a building? The 'Big Dig' highway project seems to be a constant source of reconstruction and corruption and the whole thing is underground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T01:44:45-07:00","id":930745,"title":"","content":"Big Dig can work if it need architects supervision - I'm using Faustina as interested geomancer in the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T07:09:01-07:00","id":930830,"title":"","content":"I live in Brighton =). The Government Center T station was just refurbished over the spring, and it's not finished yet. There are still a lot of bags of concrete and sand, and an area fenced off directly outside the station. It's right outside City Hall. I could take photos for you sometime this weekend, if that would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:31:13-07:00","id":931215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922815-boston-inspirations-and-music?p=930830#post930830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could take photos for you sometime this weekend, if that would help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be cool! Even when I look more for the Boston proper things - both <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>and <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> have Sanctums in Beacon Hill. In story probably also <i>White Putnams</i> will take part, so Back Bay also is taken in consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T10:42:53-07:00","id":932086,"title":"","content":"When I lived in Boston (around 2008-2012) it seemed like the Boston Public Library in Back Bay was always under construction. Great building, very atmospheric.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: &quot;Faneuil&quot; rhymes with &quot;Daniel.&quot; Don't screw it up, or eternal shame will be yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T21:35:02-07:00","id":932384,"title":"","content":"Was surfing around youtube and happened upon this; donno how inspirational it might be, but I'd say if you're setting a city there it's worth a lookover for funsies and spurr imagination.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j0dwzy2RpWg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j0dwzy2RpWg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j0dwzy2RpWg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j0dwzy2RpWg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:05:34-07:00","id":936261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/922815-boston-inspirations-and-music?p=931215#post931215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would be cool! Even when I look more for the Boston proper things - both <i>Illuminated Pentad </i>and <i>Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth</i> have Sanctums in Beacon Hill. In story probably also <i>White Putnams</i> will take part, so Back Bay also is taken in consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the delay! I have those photos. Would it be more useful for me to post them here, or to get them to you some other way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T05:46:27-07:00","id":936503,"title":"","content":"Post them here - so whole forum can use it. Also, I return to topic when preparing games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T07:14:24-07:00","id":938814,"title":"","content":"MIT (and surrounding Tech Square) is *always* under construction. They call it a &quot;living campus&quot; for that reason. There is always something being torn down or a new building being built. Whether it's a new laboratory or they're renovating a 100-year old building or just tearing down a condemned dormitory, there is a crane somewhere and something is getting gutted. They also have a lot of buildings by famous architects and are very avant-garde in the architectural department.<br /> <br /> I spent a lot of time there if you're curious and have any questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:09:12-07:00","id":958650,"title":"","content":"With <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=828777#post828777\">political changes I made for the 2E Boston <b>Mage</b> setting</a>, I need to find new place in proper City to make meetings of Consilium Council. Previous was Cormant House in Salem, when <i>Neamen</i> ruled Pentacle. But with his passing, most Boston Awakened would want to ruled from their city, not Salem.<br /> <br /> Have any good idea on location in Boston good for secret meetings of clique of powerful mages? Maybe something with weird tale or two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}